== status.sh 0.5 title table (#433)
  ok   the fixture renders (status.sh --print exits 0)
  ok   ...and writes the page
  ok   every row carries exactly one status word from the scale, and each stage renders as itself
  ok   Benchmarked N / 145 and Playable M / 50 are the rows' counts
  ok   fixed columns: no title or next step past two lines at 360 or 400 px; short tokens never wrap
  ok   nothing in the 0.5 section is shortened (no ellipsis; every title and next step in full)
  ok   the pipeline is four labelled columns (Copied, Inputs, Save, Bench) with a legend; one-route titles count
  ok   the target line says 145 and 50 and carries no date
  ok   '~2026-09-28' is not on the page
  ok   the 'not copied' tail folds after 10 rows, with its count
  ok   a verdict with no name or title_id lands in its title's row, by the ISO's title-ID prefix
  ok   red first, then from the most advanced stage down
  ok   the header forecasts from the last 48 h rate
  ok   each issue shows its state and what is in flight; an unowned open one is an alarm
  ok   Q4 shows the device watchdog's word and last hour; a stale watchdog is lane.local's alarm
  ok   a no-save record stands in for a save, with its reason; without it the save is still asked for
  ok   title_verdict.py finds a title by its ISO's title-ID prefix, and only a registered one
  ok   release-0.5.toml at docs/testing is the default and states 145 and 50
