== hdd split: a title run boots the titles disk; hdd.img stays the discs'
  ok   fixtures: a device hdd.img with two titles' saves
  ok   the first title run's disk is prepared (rc=0)
  ok     ... by seed, build, keep (got: seed build keep)
  ok     ... hddPath now names titles.qcow2 (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/titles.qcow2)
  ok     ... the device's titles.qcow2 is the pushed image (registry sha256)
  ok     ... result's sha256_at_start is the device file's
  ok     ... and it is mode 660, not the 0644 a push leaves (got: 660)
  ok     ... no titles.qcow2.new is left behind
  ok     ... the seed carried both of hdd.img's saves onto it
  ok     ... hdd.img itself was not changed
  ok     ... the marker holds the hddPath it replaced
  ok   after the run: the new title's save is harvested into the store
  ok     ... the registry knows the device file's new sha256
  ok     ... hddPath is back on hdd.img (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/hdd.img)
  ok     ... the prefs file is byte-identical to before the run
  ok     ... the marker is gone
  ok   a request with no marker makes no adb call for hddPath
  ok   the second run rebuilds from the store: build, keep (got: build keep)
  ok     ... its disk carries the two seeded goldens
  ok     ... and not the save the last run made
  ok     ... which is in the store as Ghoulies' latest, not its golden
  ok     ... and is the image the registry says was pushed
  ok     ... mode 660 (got: 660)
  ok     ... an untouched disk is not pulled after the run
== hdd split: a kept 0644 titles disk is made 660 before the run
  ok   a 0644 disk the store still matches is kept (rc=0, plans: keep)
  ok     ... and made 660 (got: 660)
  ok     ... its bytes untouched
  ok     ... hdd.json records the mode it found
  ok   a disk that cannot be made 660 fails the prepare, not the run (rc=1)
  ok     ... before hddPath is pointed at it (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/hdd.img)
== hdd split: a failed hddPath read-back still leaves the way back
  ok   a lost read-back fails the prepare (rc=1)
  ok     ... the write did land: hddPath names titles.qcow2 (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/titles.qcow2)
  ok     ... and the marker already holds hdd.img
  ok     ... so the next request's restore puts hdd.img back (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/hdd.img)
  ok     ... byte for byte
  ok   hddPath found on titles.qcow2 is never recorded as the one to put back
  ok     ... the run after it ends on hdd.img (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/hdd.img)
  ok   a marker naming titles.qcow2 restores hdd.img (got: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.jreinach.hakux.debug/files/x1box/hdd.img)
== hdd split: plan() never rebuilds over an unharvested disk
  ok   a changed disk is harvested before anything else
  ok   a disk whose last harvest failed is preserved whole, not kept and booted
  ok     ... at any size
  ok   a clean disk past the cap is rebuilt
  ok   a clean disk under the cap is kept
  ok   a disk missing from the device is rebuilt
  ok   HAKUX_TITLES_DISK=0: the split is off, recorded, and no adb call is made
  ok   a request's env HAKUX_TITLES_DISK=1 beats the worker's 0
  ok     ... and a request that names none stays off
  ok     ... a request's 0 beats a worker with the split on
== hdd split: hdd.img past its limit is reset through saves.py reset
  ok   under the limit the guard does nothing
  ok   over the limit hdd.img is reset
  ok     ... the original is kept on the device as hdd.img.bak-auto
  ok     ... the new hdd.img is mode 660, or the disc runs die as #622's title runs did
  ok     ... the new hdd.img is not the old one
  ok     ... and every save on it survived
== hdd split: a failed reset is not retried on the same disk
  ok   no room for the backup: an alert
  ok     ... and the partial hdd.img.bak-auto is removed
  ok     ... the failure is recorded against the disk
  ok     ... the next request writes the alert again, marked repeat
  ok     ... without pulling or hashing the disk
  ok   a disk saves.py refuses: an alert
  ok     ... not retried while the disk is unchanged
  ok     ... a write to hdd.img re-arms the guard
== hdd split: serve_one calls it where the runs are
  ok   restore, prepare, soak, after, then guard before the disc runs (got: restore_hdd_pref titles_disk_prepare restore_hdd_pref soak_title.sh titles_disk_after hdd_img_guard run_disc.sh )
